# Normalise line endings so the working tree matches CI everywhere.
# Without this, a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true) rewrites every
# source file to CRLF while CI stays LF. Any tool that reasons about
# source TEXT then disagrees with CI: stripping // comments with a
# dot-based regex silently stops stripping, because a dot does not match
# a carriage return. That is a real, reproducible test failure.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending normalised.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp3   binary
*.ogg   binary
*.wav   binary
*.zip   binary
